@startuml
title Proof of Collaboration (PoCol) Miner Leaving Sequence
skinparam dpi 180
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
participant "Miner A" as A
participant "Miner B" as B
participant "Miner C (leaving miner)" as C
participant "Blockchain ledger" as L

C -> C: Decide to leave the network as a registered miner\nand create a deregistration transaction containing:\n- identifier of Miner C\n- network address of Miner C\n- digital signature of Miner C over the deregistration message\n- timestamp or block height
C -> A: Send deregistration transaction of Miner C to Miner A
A -> A: Validate deregistration transaction of Miner C:\n- verify digital signature of Miner C\n- verify that Miner C is currently in the registered miner set\nIf valid, add deregistration transaction of Miner C\nto the local mempool of Miner A
A -> B: Relay validated deregistration transaction of Miner C to Miner B
A -> C: Optionally relay back for confirmation or redundancy
B -> B: Validate deregistration transaction of Miner C:\n- verify digital signature of Miner C\n- verify that Miner C is currently in the registered miner set\nIf valid, add deregistration transaction of Miner C\nto the local mempool of Miner B
C -> C: Add own deregistration transaction\nto the local mempool of Miner C (if not already stored)
A -> A: <color:red>All registered miners derive the same canonical block template for the</color>\n<color:red>next round; its ordered transaction list includes the deregistration</color>\n<color:red>transaction of Miner C and the predetermined reward-distribution</color>\n<color:red>transaction, and every miner verifies the same TemplateID before mining</color>
A -> A: Apply the PoCol nonce distribution function and perform the\ncollaborative proof-of-work search together with the other miners,\n<color:red>each miner computing H(TemplateHeader || nonce) only for nonce values</color>\n<color:red>in its own disjoint assigned range, until a valid nonce is found</color>
A -> A: <color:red>The winner (here Miner A) publishes the already committed block template</color>\n<color:red>together with the winning nonce; no transaction is created or modified</color>\n<color:red>after the nonce is found</color>
A -> B: Broadcast the committed block containing the deregistration\ntransaction of Miner C to Miner B
A -> C: Broadcast the committed block containing the deregistration\ntransaction of Miner C to Miner C
B -> B: Verify the received block from Miner A:\n<color:red>- verify that the TemplateID equals the committed one and that no</color>\n<color:red>  template field was modified</color>\n- verify proof of work for the block header and nonce\n<color:red>- verify that the winning nonce lies in the assigned range of Miner A</color>\n- verify validity of all transactions in the block\n- verify that the deregistration transaction of Miner C is valid\nIf valid, accept the block as the next block in the local blockchain
C -> C: Verify the received block from Miner A in the same way,\nincluding its own deregistration transaction\nIf valid, accept the block as the next block in the local blockchain
A -> A: Verify the constructed block again for consistency\nand accept it as the next block in the local blockchain
A -> L: Append the new block containing the deregistration transaction of Miner C\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner A
B -> L: Append the new block containing the deregistration transaction of Miner C\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner B
C -> L: Append the new block containing the deregistration transaction of Miner C\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner C
A -> A: Read the updated blockchain state from the local blockchain ledger\nand update the registered miner set by removing Miner C;\nnew registered miner set now contains Miner A and Miner B only
B -> B: Read the updated blockchain state from the local blockchain ledger\nand update the registered miner set by removing Miner C;\nnew registered miner set now contains Miner A and Miner B only
C -> C: Read the updated blockchain state from the local blockchain ledger\nand recognize that Miner C has been removed from the registered miner set;\nstop participating in future Proof of Collaboration consensus rounds
A -> A: For the next consensus round, use the updated registered miner set\nthat contains Miner A and Miner B only as input to\nthe Proof of Collaboration nonce distribution function
B -> B: For the next consensus round, use the updated registered miner set\nthat contains Miner A and Miner B only as input to\nthe Proof of Collaboration nonce distribution function
@enduml
